              DIGITAL SELECTED AS VIDEO SERVER SUPPLIER
                      FOR NYNEX MANHATTAN TRIAL


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 2, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
announced today that it has been selected to supply its video and 
interactive information server platform for use in a NYNEX Inc. 
video-on-demand trial in Manhattan.  This is the second NYNEX pilot 
for which Digital is providing its video server solutions.

     The NYNEX Manhattan trial will use Digital's server to provide 
customers with video-on-demand, home shopping, and other interactive 
programs.  The trial is expected to include up to 800 customers by 
the end of 1994.

     In the pilot program, Digital's server will store programming 
in a NYNEX central office for delivery on-demand.  The first 
programs delivered from Digital's video and interactive information 
server will be provided by Advanced Research & Technologies, Inc., 
Liberty Cable, and Urban Transport Corp.  The on-demand offerings 
represent the second phase of NYNEX's one-year video-tone trial, a 
test of the broadband network that NYNEX expects to deploy 
throughout the Northeastern U.S. over the next decade.

     "This announcement, along with our relationships with NYNEX in 
Rhode Island, Telecom Australia, U S West and USA Video, further 
establishes Digital as the global leader in video and interactive 
information solutions," said Charles F. Christ, vice president of 
Digital's Storage Business Unit and the company's Video and 
Interactive Information Services group.  "Because Digital's video 
and interactive information server is a modular, open, 
standards-based system, it will enable NYNEX to expand its trials 
easily and cost-effectively, and meet growing deployment needs."

     Digital's video and interactive information server meets the 
requirements of all-digital broadband infrastructures that support a 
range of interactive services, such as video-on-demand, multimedia 
communications, games, home shopping, and education.  The technology 
incorporates Digital's powerful Alpha AXP processors, StorageWorks 
disk storage arrays, Digital Linear Tape (DLT) library subsystems, 
an interactive gateway unit, a server management unit, and 
GIGAswitch, a high-speed networking switch linking the various 
elements.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable AXP platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
