          DIGITAL AND DELL EXPAND DISTRIBUTION RELATIONSHIP


            Digital's High-Performance DLT Tape Products
           to be Incorporated into Dell PowerEdge Servers


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 10, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
Dell Computer Corporation today announced that Dell will sell 
Digital's high-performance DLT tape drive products with Dell's 
PowerEdge line of servers for resource sharing and database 
environments.  Digital will immediately begin shipments of its
DLT2000 20 GB tape drive and DLT2700 140 GB, 7-cartridge mini-
library to Dell.

     "We are excited to have Dell add the DLT2000 and DLT2700 to its 
well-respected line of PowerEdge servers," said Jack Sharp, business 
manager of Digital's OEM Storage Business.  "This agreement expands 
our relationship with Dell, which, over the past two years, also has 
included supplying our high-performance magnetic drives for Dell's 
file server and desktop systems."

     "The recently introduced Dell PowerEdge servers have many new 
mainframe class features for business-critical applications.  The 
Digital DLT tape drive is another feature that distinguishes Dell's 
capabilities from typical server companies," said Dennis Passovoy, 
vice president of Dell advanced systems. "With the combination of 
the Dell PowerEdge advanced servers and industry-leading Digital DLT 
tape products, customers are able to meet the capacity and reliability 
requirements of heavy duty cycle applications such as network server 
backup devices, midrange applications, multimedia and on-line 
transaction processing (OLTP).  The DLT drives also provide customers 
with reliable, unattended backup and are well-positioned to meet the 
requirements of increasingly popular applications such as hierarchical 
storage management (HSM) and near-line storage."

     With four times the capacity and three times the performance of 
comparably-priced helical scan devices, Digital's DLT drive is an 
ideal solution for today's data-intensive, networked environments.  
DLT drives feature five times the drive life of other tape 
technologies and provides superior data integrity.  These features 
and their respective benefits have made DLT drives an emerging 
industry standard.

     A Fortune 500 Company, Dell Computer Corporation (NASDAQ: DELL) 
designs, develops, manufactures, markets, services and supports a 
complete line of personal computers compatible with industry 
standards.  Dell pioneered the direct marketing of PCs in 1984 and 
was the first company in the PC industry to offer manufacturer-
