              DIGITAL EQUIPMENT STORAGEWORKS SUBSYSTEMS
           EXPAND SCSI CONNECTIVITY, EXTEND RAID SOFTWARE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 9, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced a new StorageWorks subsystem controller to increase 
locally attached SCSI disk connectivity and extend I/O performance.

     The HSZ40 StorageWorks Array Controller allows up to 42 
industry-standard SCSI-2 disk devices to be connected to a single 
SCSI port, expanding local disk storage to support applications and 
user growth.  The HSZ40 StorageWorks Array Controller is supported 
on Digital OSF/1 AXP V2.0, with OpenVMS AXP support planned for the 
near future.

     At the same time, Digital introduced StorageWorks RAID Software
for OpenVMS, V2.0, extending host-based RAID software to the OpenVMS 
environment.  This release adds RAID level O(disk striping) and 
partitioning of storage arrays into multiple 'virtual disks' for 
easier system management to the OpenVMS cluster environment.  

     According to Kirby Wadsworth, Digital's StorageWorks Product 
Management Manager, "These two capabilities further address customer
demands for scalable storage solutions supported across multiple
platforms using industry-standards and common interconnects. 
Combined with our industry-standard StorageWorks devices and unique, 
modular packaging, these new offerings provide customers with the 
performance improvements and increased capacity levels they require 
to meet their storage systems demands."

