                   DIGITAL NAMES SIX FINALISTS IN
                     ADVERTISING AGENCY SEARCH


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 18, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today named six advertising agencies as finalists in the search to 
identify strategic agency resources to further support and integrate 
its worldwide branding efforts. The six finalists named are 
Berlin/Wright/Cameron, DDB Needham, GSD&M, Lowe & Partners/SFS, 
Messner Vetere Berger McNamee Schmetterer, and Ogilvy & Mather.  The 
company stated that a number of strategic agencies were identified 
and considered as part of the overall review process.

     "We are very enthusiastic about all the submissions we have 
seen," said Charlie Holleran, vice president, Communications.  "Each 
finalist demonstrated a unique mix of competencies throughout the 
review process in regard to creative excellence, strategic and 
innovative thinking, as well as the ability to communicate and 
implement corporate vision and positioning internationally." 

     The six agencies were identified following an extensive 
evaluation, in which each agency presented representative strategic 
and creative work, as well as a comprehensive screening process.  
Each participant was measured against specific criteria, outlined 
as follows:

     o 	have established strategic and creative reputations for the 
        development, establishment and growth of succinct, unique 
        positioning of corporate and business unit brands 
        internationally

     o 	have the resources and talent to develop differentiating 
        campaigns -- business-to-business, as well as corporate 
        image and brand

     o 	have demonstrated the ability to establish relevant, 
        emotional, and functional customer benefits for brands

     The company stated its intent to have its strategic agency 
resources identified and in place by early summer.  Each finalist 
will be compensated for their submissions and participation.  
Holleran concluded, "All six finalists represent high caliber firms 
with whom Digital would be proud to partner." 

