                 DIGITAL AND BMC SOFTWARE TO PROVIDE
                   DATABASE MANAGEMENT INTEGRATION


     ... Integration of POLYCENTER Manager on NetView and PATROL
              for management of distributed systems ...



SAN FRANCISCO, CA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and BMC Software, Inc. announced today an agreement to integrate 
BMC Software's PATROL product, an automated database monitoring and 
systems management tool, with Digital's POLYCENTER Manager on 
NetView software and upcoming DEC DBA Workcenter software. As a 
result, customers will have built-in support for managing and 
monitoring heterogeneous, distributed databases from their 
POLYCENTER Manager on NetView environment. Databases to be 
supported include DEC Rdb, ORACLE, SYBASE, INFORMIX and INGRES.

     An advance version of the integrated products is being 
demonstrated here this week at DB/EXPO.

     "This integrated solution sets Digital and BMC squarely in the 
lead with a solution to the complex problems of enterprise 
management -- managing distributed, heterogeneous computing 
environments including systems, networks and databases," said Mark 
O'Connell, Digital's marketing director, Software Products.

     "The marketplace today is demanding technology that 
facilitates centralized management and control of all distributed 
systems," said Russ Caccamisi, vice president of marketing for BMC 
Software. "By integrating our PATROL technology with POLYCENTER 
Manager on NetView and DEC DBA Workcenter, customers will now be 
able to monitor and manage their database servers as efficiently as 
they manage other aspects of their distributed networks." 

Smooth Migration to SNMP Management

     When integrated with POLYCENTER Manager on NetView, database 
actions and alarms generated by PATROL will be selectively 
propagated to the POLYCENTER Manager on NetView management console. 
This customized monitoring allows network or systems managers using 
POLYCENTER Manager on NetView to determine the type and level of 
critical database activity they want to monitor within the 
POLYCENTER Manager on NetView environment, leaving detailed 
database systems management for database administrators using 
PATROL and DEC DBA Workcenter.  

     In addition, PATROL agents will act as SNMP agents that can be 
managed by other SNMP applications, providing an easy migration 
path to the future SNMP Management Information Base (MIB) for 
databases.

Combining the Best of Both Worlds

     POLYCENTER Manager on NetView is Digital's software framework 
for network and systems management. POLYCENTER Manager on NetView 
provides integrated applications for discovery and management of 
network devices, storage management, job scheduling, consolidated 
management of remote servers and clients from multiple vendors, and 
system administration features.

     BMC's PATROL product uses intelligent programmable agents and 
loadable libraries of expertise to monitor and manage distributed 
databases and systems. As part of the DEC DBA Workcenter product 
set, PATROL provides automated event management for distributed, 
heterogeneous databases within the POLYCENTER Manager on NetView 
environment, as well as a centralized graphical interface for 
systems managers, network analysts and database administrators.

     DEC DBA Workcenter software provides an integrated set of 
tools for single-point management of multiple, heterogeneous 
database management systems across client/server networks.

Availability

     DEC DBA Workcenter with integrated PATROL software will be 
available on OpenVMS for VAX, OpenVMS for AXP, and DEC OSF/1 
operating systems in September.  Future releases will include 
support for Windows and Windows NT.   

     BMC Software, Inc. is a leading developer and vendor of 
systems software products that facilitate the management and 
movement of mission-critical data. Headquartered in Houston, the 
company currently offers products around the world that support 
Digital and UNIX platforms, as well as IBM's IMS, DB2, CICS, VTAM 
and SNA systems.

