                DIGITAL DEMONSTRATES WORLD'S FASTEST
             RELATIONAL DATABASE AND OPEN CLIENT/SERVER
                       INTEGRATION CAPABILITIES


SAN FRANCISCO, CA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
is highlighting at DB/EXPO 94 this week the most advanced open 
client/server database and integration technologies from Digital and 
its partners. Included are DEC Rdb, the world's fastest database 
software, and the newly announced integrated database management 
capabilities of Digital's POLYCENTER Manager on NetView software 
(see separate release).

     Digital's expertise in building and managing enterprise-wide 
open client/server solutions, from the desktop to high-end 
production systems, includes complete consulting services as well as 
enabling software.

     "Digital's role in the software industry is to provide 
frameworks that enable customers to integrate all the components 
they choose to meet their very specific business needs," said Mark 
F. O'Connell, Digital's marketing director, Software Products. 
"Digital's open client/server software frameworks provide the 
architecture and tools to solve the most fundamental problems in 
client/server computing through the integration of products from 
Digital and its business partners."  

     Digital's software frameworks provide a holistic approach to 
the full range of customers' needs for implementing client/server 
solutions. Software integration frameworks demonstrated here this 
week include:
     
     Data Integration - making information in multiple 
     databases such as DEC Rdb, ORACLE and SYBASE available 
     to multiple desktop users across UNIX, Macintosh and 
     Windows client/server environments, without affecting 
     the end-user application, database, or integrity of the 
     information.

     Production Integration - tying business-critical 
     applications into operation management systems such as 
     inventory control, warehousing and customer service.

     Management Integration - managing distributed, 
     multivendor applications, data, clients, servers and 
     networks across the organization with Digital's 
     POLYCENTER management portfolio.

     In addition to the show floor demonstrations,  Digital's Dr. 
Jim Gray will join the Database Industry Leaders Forum on May 25th 
at 9:45 a.m. and Digital's database product manager, Mike Zagurek, 
will present "Multimedia Database in the Information Superhighway" 
on May 24th at 11:45 a.m. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
