                   DIGITAL NAMES VINCENT MULLARKEY
                       CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER


MAYNARD, MA -- May 26, 1994 -- Robert B. Palmer, president and chief 
executive officer of Digital Equipment Corporation, today announced 
that Vincent J. Mullarkey, 46, has been named vice president and 
chief financial officer, effective immediately. Mullarkey, who was 
corporate controller, succeeds William M. Steul, 51, who has 
resigned from the company to pursue other interests.

     "Digital is making steady progress toward the resumption of 
sustained profitability," said Palmer. "The appointment of Vin 
Mullarkey, with his strong background in financial management and 
controls, is consistent with our determination to concentrate on 
accelerating that progress.  It is one of an ongoing series of steps 
we are taking to strengthen our management team.  Vin brings a 
record of high energy and broad business perspective to his new 
assignment." 

     Palmer added, "I have worked closely with him, not only in the 
last year and a half, but also when Vin served as controller in 
Digital's semiconductor operations and the manufacturing and 
logistics operations.  He has a comprehensive approach to financial 
controls, and demonstrates predictability and financial accuracy.  
Most important at this critical time, Vin has an extensive knowledge 
of the company's worldwide businesses, having held financial 
management positions that cover our operations in Europe, Asia, and 
the Americas. 

     Mullarkey earned a bachelor of science degree in Accounting and 
Finance from Bentley College in 1971, and is a graduate of the 
University of Michigan Executive Development Program.

     Commenting on Steul's departure, Palmer stated, "We are 
grateful for Bill's long and loyal service to Digital. The company 
has benefitted significantly from his many accomplishments. We wish 
him success in his future endeavors."

