              DIGITAL, INSIGNIA SOLUTIONS IN AGREEMENT
        TO SUPPORT WINDOWS APPLICATIONS ON ALPHA AXP PLATFORM


          ... Wealth of Windows software to run on world's
                     fastest computer family...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May  27, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced an agreement with Insignia Solutions, Inc. to 
jointly market Insignia's SoftWindows software, allowing thousands 
for MS-DOS and Windows applications to run on Digital's Alpha AXP 
family of workstations and servers.  

     "Customers are looking to run their mission critical 
applications on our Alpha AXP workstations and servers, but many are 
now running their personal productivity applications on a PC," said 
John O'Keefe, vice president, UNIX Systems Marketing.  "SoftWindows 
software gives them the industry's highest level of performance for 
their key applications, and provides the same level of personal 
applications performance they are experiencing today on their 
486-based personal computers, all in a single desktop system." 

     SoftWindows integrates into virtually any networking 
environment familiar to PC users, including LanManager, NetWare, 
TCP/IP and DECnet. It can be managed by all of the traditional 
management tools available including Digital's new MANAGEworX 
software.  Both MS-DOS 6.0 and MS-Windows 3.1, the most common 
combination of PC operating system and user-environment software, 
are built in, making SoftWindows completely familiar to the PC user.

     SoftWindows will be sold and marketed by both Digital Equipment
Corporation and Insignia Solutions Inc.  Being used in a number of
test sites now, SoftWindows will be generally available for 
Digital's UNIX systems in mid-summer, and for OpenVMS systems in 
the fall.

