               BERNHARD AUER REPLACES PESATORI AS HEAD
            OF DIGITAL'S PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 27, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation has 
announced that Bernhard Auer has been appointed vice president and 
general manager of the company's Personal Computer Business Unit, 
effective immediately.  He succeeds and will continue to report to 
Digital vice president Enrico Pesatori, who recently assumed the 
additional responsibility for the Systems Business Unit and the 
worldwide sales and marketing organization.  

     Auer, 53, has served as vice president and general manager of 
the European operations of the Personal Computer Business Unit for 
the past year.

     In his new role, Auer is responsible for all aspects of the 
business unit, worldwide, including product strategy and 
development, manufacturing and logistics, marketing, distribution 
and sales.

     "Digital PC business is now a profitable and growing force in 
the worldwide market, rapidly moving toward our goal of becoming a 
top PC vendor by 1995.  This business segment, and others like it, 
will help accelerate Digital's return to profitability," said Robert 
Palmer, president and chief executive officer.  "With Bernhard's 
appointment, we have taken another step in the ongoing strengthening 
of our management team.  I am confident he will continue Digital's 
considerable momentum in this important industry segment." 

     "During the past year, Bernhard has demonstrated an outstanding 
track record of achievement in the intensely competitive PC 
business," Pesatori stated.  "Under his leadership in Europe, we 
have attracted industry talent to lead our marketing and country 
management organizations, we now have thousands of resellers 
offering Digital PCs across Europe, and our unit shipments have 
grown by well over 100 percent -- making Digital the fastest growing 
major PC company in Europe."

     Before joining Digital, Auer spent three years as vice 
president, managing director of the general business group of Compaq 
Europe.  Previously, he spent 23 years with IBM in senior line and 
staff management position across Europe, in operations, sales and 
marketing. 

     A native of Munich, Germany, Auer will be relocating from 
Digital's European headquarters in Geneva to Massachusetts.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Alpha AXP platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
